# ── macOS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
._*

# ── Obsidian / Claudian local state ────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.obsidian/workspace.json
**/.claudian/sessions/
.$*.bkp

# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/credentials
**/*.pem
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*

# ── Presentations: large regenerable binaries ──────────────────────────────────
# ~81 MB of .pptx and .png, two files at 40 MB each. Regenerable from
# generate_presentations.py. Binary diffs are meaningless and every revision
# would add another full copy to history forever. Same reasoning EAIE uses to
# exclude its 125-180 MB manuscript PDFs.
Presentations/PowerPoint/
Presentations/First/
Presentations/Figures_Extra/
*.pptx
*.key

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# ── Terraform (starter kits / sample solutions carry .tf files) ────────────────
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
!**/*.tfvars.example

# ── Reference implementation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The live repo at ~/northstar-ai-platform is authoritative and has its own
# GitHub remote. The copy that used to live under Sample Solutions/ drifted out
# of sync (different .gitignore, missing Dockerfile.terraform, case-mismatched
# requirements files). Do not re-add a copy here — see docs/GitHub Integration.md.
CS_401R_Labs/Sample Solutions/northstar-ai-platform/

# ── Published output (generated by scripts/publish_student_repo.sh) ────────────
.publish-staging/

# ── Canvas build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build/ is 143 MB of generated chapter PDFs and is byte-identical to
# Efforts/Projects/Active/EAIE/Build/canvas_chapters/ — verified 2026-08-06.
# Canvas is a derived artifact; the source of truth is CS_401R_Labs/*.md and
# course_config.yaml. PDFs are binary, so git stores a full copy on every
# rebuild with no delta compression: committing this would add 143 MB per
# build to a 14 MB repo, permanently, and could only be undone with a history
# rewrite. Regenerate with `python build_course.py --stage 2 --rebuild`.
Build/

# Run logs — regenerated on every build, never worth diffing.
build.log
verify.log
presentations.log

# Office lock/temp files
~$*
.~lock*
